<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tabennisi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tabennisi was a village on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a>, near Dendera, where Pachomius founded the first Christian communal monastery in the 320s. The community grew quickly, and Pachomius organised a federation of monasteries under a common rule. His followers were known as Tabennesiots, and the site is regarded as a birthplace of communal monasticism.</p></div>
